WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.100
Hey, just as a change of pace, a little levity,
this is kind of funny and interesting.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:09.250
Many of you know that on this program I've
been smeared by homophobic people for a long

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.230
time because I support LGBT rights.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.000
We also have funny stories like when producer
Louis was the producer of the David Pakman

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.649
show, I got an email from, uh, from a gentleman
saying, Hey David, it's so great that you

00:00:21.649 --> 00:00:25.769
and your partner, uh, are doing a show together.

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:28.570
Um, how long have you and Louis been together?

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.919
My husband and I would love to have you guys
over our place for dinner.

00:00:31.919 --> 00:00:36.129
And as funny as the idea was, if not telling
Lewis the pretense and going over as a supposed

00:00:36.129 --> 00:00:38.530
coupled to dinner at someone's house, we didn't
do that.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.300
And I clarified Lewis and I are not only not
together, we exclusively date women.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.670
I am personally not gay, but I support gay
rights.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.920
I'm a straight ally.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.160
We've been straight allies on this program
for more than a decade.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:53.129
But over the years there have been both misunderstandings
and smears about this.

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:57.269
So one example is that a few years ago I was
featured in a documentary called Minnesota

00:00:57.269 --> 00:00:58.269
nice.

00:00:58.269 --> 00:01:04.159
Uh, the documentary is about anti-gay bullying
suicides and that's a horribly tragic subject.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:08.620
But I was featured as a gay teen who committed
suicide after being bullied.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:15.020
And I had to clarify, I'm not a teenager,
I'm not gay, I wasn't bullied and I'm alive.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:19.130
And it has been brought to my attention that
once again there is a reference on my Wikipedia

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:21.780
page to I suppose that relationship with a
man.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:22.780
Check this out.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:27.290
This was added to the personal life section
recently saying quote, in November, 2015,

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:31.960
Pacman moved to New York city, breaking up
with his longterm male partner, which go incited

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.409
with a relocation of the David Pakman show
his production.

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:39.200
This one is subtle, but someone did add a
note that said citation needed.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.880
Apparently they realized there was no citation
for that claim and they've not been able to

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:48.170
find one because it is a completely bogus
claim, so it would be inappropriate for me

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.340
to go in and edit the Wikipedia page.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.659
The subjects of Wiki pages aren't supposed
to edit those pages themselves.

00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:55.860
I think that makes a lot of sense.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:01.259
Could be a conflict of interest, but I'm asking
for your help to update my Wikipedia page

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:02.740
and also help expand it.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.140
I feel like it could be far more robust based
on what the David Pakman show has become over

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.140
the years.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:14.140
This is funny in a way, but the obsession
with smearing me as a gay man is not only

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:18.010
sort of getting boring, I don't actually understand
the obsession with it.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.080
Like what is so appealing about that?

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:22.200
Maybe somebody can explain it to me.

